  _caveat: "Sensitivity grades rest on snippet/abstract-level reads of the cited papers plus HYPE documentation; publisher full text returned HTTP 403/429 and could not be fetched, so no edge carries a recorded numeric index (no Sobol St, Morris rank, EFAST main effect, or explicit variance ranking value). HIGH grades retained on four edges (wcep->cout, wcep->soil runoff, rivvel->discharge peak timing, cevp->PET) are ranking-derived from Brendel 2023's multi-objective PEST sensitivity (wcep rank-1; rivvel/cevp among most sensitive), not index-quantified. Snowmelt edges (ttmp, cmlt) are time-variant: HIGH only within melt windows, lower in long-term aggregate. Codex verification of the Brendel rank-1 claim was attempted but timed out (inconclusive); no edge is promoted to HIGH beyond what the recorded ranking-language summaries support."
